  mLocalizedStringsValues:
  - Main Quest
  - All of the interactions that are a part of the main quest to get the objects
    for the boat
  - 'Scene 1: Intro to Quest'
  - Marie wakes up in bed to Max bothering her, tutorial of movement, and introduction
    to quest
  - 'Scene 3: Boat Building Scene'
  - Marie arrives to the beach with all the materials and tries to build it. Max
    steps in and saves the day
  - 'Scene 2: Collecting Items for Boat'
  - Marie collects items to build the boat from Arrnold, Jane, and Grumpy Joe
  - NPC Interactions
  - All interactions with NPC that aren't a part of the main quest
  - Interactions with Arrnold
  - If you talk to him after the main quest interaction
  - Interactions with Grumpy Joe
  - If you talk to him after the main quest interaction
  - Interactions with Jane
  - If you talk to her after the main quest interaction
  - Interactions with Joele
  - Interactions with Rosei
  - 
  - Interactions with Viola
  - Hey!! Mar-oh...of course you're still asleep...
  - "Don\u2019t tell me you forgot!"
  - Wake up, lazy bones!
  - Forgot what?
  - "Of course not! I\u2019d never forget that today is\u2026uh\u2026"
  - "Marieeeeeeeeee\u2026"
  - " I can\u2019t believe you sometimes. The ISLAND BOAT RACE! It\u2019s today!
    They\u2019re giving a trophy to whoever wins - and it HAS to be us!"
  - ' MARIE!!!'
  - " Oh, yeah? Where\u2019s our boat?"
  - "Good grief! It sure took you long enough to wake up. Don\u2019t you remember
    what day it is?!"
  - "\u2026That\u2019s what we\u2019re working on today. But I\u2019m not worried
    about it! We\u2019ll make it happen. You and me, we make a great team."
  - "Quick! Get on your feet! We\u2019ve gotta get to work!"
  - "It won\u2019t take us very long! We just need to get stuff to build with. I\u2019m
    thinking we\u2019ll need wood, string, and canvas. Can you ask around town to
    see if anyone can help us out?"
  - " I remember this day\u2026why am I back here?"
  - "Well? What\u2019re you waiting for?"
  - "whatdoweneedtogetprobablywoodmaybesomecanvasmaybesomeuhhhhh\u2026"
  - "Wow, he\u2019s not here yet? I\u2019m the one doing the leg work too, ugh"
  - ...!
  - "Hmm, well Max isn\u2019t here to build the boat\u2026and I have the supplies
    to build the boat\u2026and the tools to build the boat\u2026"
  - Might as well give it a go!
  - ' Marie? What are you doing?'
  - AHH-
  - OH MY GOD-
  - WHEN DID YOU GET THERE?!?!
  - Uh...just a second ago. Are you okay?
  - YOU BROKE MY BOAT!!!
  - Sorry... I think I ruined it.
  - Well, I dunno why you tried to do it alone. It's a job for two people. We'll
    rebuild it together.
  - Hmph... you better.
  - 
  - What's that on the side of it?
  - Ugh... Marie, did you have to carve a bird into it? It looks weird.
  - Well I think it's cute!
  - It's just to spite you.
  - I mean... if you say so. It looks more like a rat to me.
  - Oh whatever! I went and got all the materials, so I'll draw what I want on it.
  - Whatever. It looks like a rat anyway.
  - Fair enough... wanna take the rat boat for a spin?
  - Let's do it!
  - Uh, I'm not quite ready yet. Just give me a second.
  - If you say so.
  - Okay, I'm ready.
  - Finally, let's do it!
  - "Eh?? Who\u2019s that?? \u2026Oh, it\u2019s just you, Marie. Don\u2019t sneak
    up on me like that, you\u2019ll give this old man a heart attack. Ah, no matter...are
    you staying out of trouble today?"
  - Ah, you again, Marie! What is it now?
  - Max and I need wood to build a boat!
  - "What\u2019s new, Grumpy Joe?"
  - Nevermind.
  - "Now, why would you ever want to build a boat? There\u2019s nothin\u2019 out
    there in that cursed ocean. Nothin\u2019 worth seeing!"
  - To win the Boat Racing Contest, of course!
  - "What\u2019s it to you?!"
  - "Contest? Bah! You kids and your silly games. ...Tell you what, though, this
    might be your lucky day. I have some pieces of an old boat that have just been
    sitting around in my shop. Haven\u2019t been put together in years. I\u2019ve
    been looking for a chance to get rid of them. You and your brother can have them,
    under one condition..."
  - "What\u2019s that?"
  - "You take the blasted things, and don\u2019t try to give them back! Now here,
    take \u2018em and get to work!"
  - " Well! Excuse an old man for being curious! You\u2019ll surely have rotten luck
    getting any wood with that attitude!"
  - " Eh? What\u2019s new? Not much around here, I\u2019ll tell you that! Business
    at the shop is the slowest it\u2019s been in months. I\u2019m telling you, young
    people these days just can\u2019t appreciate good craftsmanship."
  - "Are you sure that\u2019s why?"
  - "Of course! I don\u2019t see what else it could be!"
  - "Bah, you kids. You think an old man\u2019s just got all the time in the world!"
  - Ah, Marie! How goes it?
  - Marie!
  - Hey!
  - "What\u2019s up?"
  - Actually, I need your help with something...
  - Sure! Whaddya need?
  - ' Do you have any spare rope I could use?'
  - "Hmm\u2026 depends what for. Ya building something?"
  - Arthur and I are doing a sailboat competition.
  - "Ah, I see. You seem uh\u2026 really excited about it."
  - "Well\u2026 I guess it was more of his idea. I\u2019d honestly forgot about it
    until this morning. But I\u2019m still going to help!"
  - "Well there\u2019s the spirit! Let me see what I have for you\u2026"
  - Alright, I found this in the attic. Is this the kinda rope you were looking for?
  - " Yes! That\u2019s perfect. Thanks Jane!"
  - Anytime. Let me know how it goes!
  - Nevermind.
  - Alrighty then!
  - I am excited about it!
  - What have you been up to today?
  - What have I been up to? Hmmm... well this mornin' I was gonna try and catch some
    fish up the north side of the beach, but...
  - But what?
  - Well, Arrnold was insisting I take Joele out on the water with me so he can "get
    a taste of adventure" or somethin' like that... but the kid turned dead pale
    at the mention of going out there. I couldn't do that to 'em! I dunno what Arrnold
    was thinking...
  - But he wasn't taking no for an answer, so I made up something about the weather
    gettin' bad all of a sudden and walked off.
  - But anyway... what're you up to?
  - Anyhow... did ya need something?
  - What's up with you, Arrnold?
  - Well, Max and I are trying to build a boat for this sailing competition across
    town... he asked me to get wood, string, and canvas?
  - Nevermind.
  - Well, I just finished feedin' the animals, and then I was just thinking...
  - You know, Marie, you remind me a lot of myself when I was your age. Always determined
    to win!
  - "Oh, I can still see that rainbow trout now\u2026that was the biggest fish I
    ever caught! \u2026It\u2019s too bad the judges were distracted by that other
    kid who caught the shark\u2026Ack! Sorry, Marie. I\u2019m off daydreaming again\u2026"
  - "Why, I remember like it was yesterday when I won the island fly-fishing tournament
    as a wee lad\u2026"
  - I'll see you around!
  - Did you need something?
  - Wow! I'm jealous... Rosei never lets me do stuff like that anymore, says it'll
    hurt my back...
  - But I do have some spare canvas for you! At least someone's putting it to use...
  - I'd give you some wood too but Rosei wants me to build her a nice new wardrobe
    this summer... hope this'll do.
  - This'll work just fine! Thanks Arrnold.
  - Hey Marie! Out for a stroll again? Weather's real nice today.
  - Just finishing up some chores!
  - Well you'd better finish quick! The day is still young...
  - Oh, hey Marie. How's my favorite student doing?
  - Good! Just finishing up that boat.
  - REALLY? Well... I suppose I could lend a hand if you're asking.
  - Um... I think it was more of a project for me and Max, but another helping hand
    couldn't hurt!
  - Sorry Arrnold, me and Max have to do this one just the two of us.
  - Ah, you know what, nevermind... I'll leave you kids to it.
  - Right, okay...
  - Say, have you or your brother ever ridden before?
  - A horse? I don't think so.
  - Well, I'd say you could ride my horse Crunchy, but he's too old. His bones would
    go crunchy the instant you got on! Ha ha!
  - Actually, a really long time ago me and Crunchy got lost in the woods. It was
    mega dark, and I was down to the last bow in my quiver.
  - And we were trotting along in the dark when suddenly- BOOM! This humungous bear
    shot out of the trees! Crunchy got scared real good, he bucked and knocked me
    clean off!
  - Nevermind.
  - So then I get up, and the instant I stand up I'm eye-to-eye with this thing.
    I slowly reached back and-
  - -BAM!! Got him straight in the eye with my last arrow. The old sucker ROARED
    and then turned tail and ran.
  - Took a while to calm Crunchy down, not sure he'd even do too well with kids like
    you and Max...
  - But anyway, that's enough of that. You got things to get to, yeah? Come back
    if you want to hear more of an old man's ramblings!
  - " I hear you and Max finished that boat project of yours! I\u2019ll give you
    kids some credit; once you\u2019ve put your mind to something, it\u2019s hard
    to stop you. I like that about you, Marie."
  - "You better get cracking to get to that contest thingamabob! It would be a shame
    if you put in all that work just to be disqualified for being late! Bah, sometimes
    you kids have no sense of urgency\u2026"
  - "That boat was nothing but trouble for me. Couldn\u2019t withstand even the calmest
    of water without sinking! Eventually I got fed up with it and just decided to
    cut it up and put the thing out of its misery. Ha! Maybe you and your brother
    will be able to build it into something better. Good luck! But be careful, y\u2019hear?"
  - "Don\u2019t you have work to do? You won\u2019t get anything built sitting around
    chatting to an old man all day! Hop to it!"
  - "Well? Did ya build the boat yet? I\u2019d like to see it when it\u2019s done,
    maybe I\u2019ll take it for a spin myself\u2026"
  - " No\u2026"
  - "Well what\u2019re you waiting for? You only got so much daylight left before
    you\u2019re building this thing in the dark."
  - "Oh, hey Marie! How\u2019d your boat turn out?"
  - It was great! Thanks for the rope.
  - "It was okay\u2026"
  - Nevermind
  - Glad to hear it! Let me know if you need anything else.
  - "Hm. Well, wasn\u2019t on account of my rope, that\u2019s for sure."
  - ...
  - ...Hi?
  - ...
  - I heard you're making a boat... good luck.
  - Thanks Mrs. Mille!
  - And when will it be done?
  - Uhh... tonight, I think.
  - Right, well make sure you don't tell Arrnold, he'll want to take over the whole
    project. He might even sail away on it himself....
  - Ah, right.
  - How was the boat contest?
  - Oh, well we haven't done the actual contest yet, we just finished building it.
  - Ah, I see. I heard Arrnold tried to get involved. What did I tell you?
  - Well you were right after all, sorry I ever doubted it.
  - ...
  - It's alright Marie, I'm not actually mad. Not with you anyway...
  - Hmph... well let me know how the contest goes.
  - Oh, Marie! What are you up to? Going sailing with Arrnold?
  - Nope, I'm just taking a walk.
  - ...I wish Joele would take after you more. Two nomad parents, and he can't stand
    a moment outside.
  - ...
  - Have you ever seen coral before?
  - Yeah
  - Nope
  - Well, you've seen more than this old woman.
  - I haven't either...
  - I might've told you this before, but the whole reason Arrnold and I moved here...
    was for the coral. I had this grand idea that everything beneath the water's
    surface would be colorful.
  - I thought you didn't like the water?
  - I don't... but I sure don't mind looking at it.
  - One time he bought me a rock and painted it, and then called it coral. Silly
    man.
  - That was before you could walk. Your brother was the one who found the rock,
    actually. He was going to give it to you, but Arrnold beat him at rock-paper-scissors...
  - Anyway, that's enough reminiscing from me. I'm going to head back to work, but
    I'm sure I'll see you around again today.
  - Marie? Ah, that is you. How are you dear? What have you been up to?
  - Great! Max and I are building a boat.
  - "Not so good\u2026"
  - "You\u2019re building a boat? How come?"
  - Max wanted to do a sailing competition on the other side of town.
  - Nevermind.
  - Um... alright honey
  - "And you\u2019ll be doing it with him?"
  - Of course!
  - "Ah, Max. Such an adventurous spirit in such a small body. I worry for him you
    know\u2026"
  - "Don\u2019t worry Miss Earnest, I\u2019ll look out for him"
  - "I know you will, you\u2019re a smart girl. Now go build that boat! I\u2019d
    like to see it when it\u2019s done."
  - "You know\u2026 I\u2019ve been worried about that Joe fellow. I have a hard time
    telling whether his face is just frozen in an angry face, or if he\u2019s actually
    just that angry all the time. That can\u2019t be good for anybody! Maybe you
    can introduce me sometime\u2026"
  - Marie
  - Max
  - Arrnold Mille
  - Rosei Mille
  - Joele Mille
  - Grumpy Joe
  - Jane
  - Viola Earnest
  mLocalizedAudioAssetsKeys: []
